      {/* 8 — This website */}
      <section class="slide" data-title="This website">
        <div class="wide">
          <p class="kicker a" style="--d:0">Your lab, open 24/7</p>
          <h2 class="title a" style="--d:1">cs-lectures.pages.dev</h2>
          <div class="cards3">
            <div class="card-x a" style="--d:2"><div class="ico">▶</div><b>Run every example</b><div>in a real Linux sandbox, from any browser — even your phone</div></div>
            <div class="card-x a" style="--d:3"><div class="ico">⚠</div><b>Crashes explained</b><div>“Killed by SIGSEGV — invalid memory access” instead of silence</div></div>
            <div class="card-x a" style="--d:4"><div class="ico">⇄</div><b>Two programs at once</b><div>server + client side by side, challenges that check your code</div></div>
          </div>
          <p class="note a" style="--d:5">Lesson 16 shows how the site does it — using only what you learn here.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* 9 — How to succeed */}
      <section class="slide" data-title="How to succeed">
        <div class="wide">
          <p class="kicker a" style="--d:0">How to do well</p>
          <h2 class="title a" style="--d:1">Systems programming is learned with your hands</h2>
          <ol class="tips">
            <li class="a" style="--d:2"><b>Type it, run it, break it.</b> Change one line and predict what happens.</li>
            <li class="a" style="--d:3"><b>Read the man pages.</b> <code>man 2 fork</code> answers most questions.</li>
            <li class="a" style="--d:4"><b>Check every return value.</b> −1 means something failed — <code>perror()</code> tells you why.</li>
